{
 "id": "amplitude-period-phase",
 "title": "Amplitude, period & phase shift",
 "summary": "Read and build sinusoids y = A sin(B(x − C)) + D from their graph features.",
 "objectives": [
  "Read amplitude, period, phase shift and midline",
  "Write an equation from its features",
  "Model a periodic situation"
 ],
 "prerequisites": [
  "sine-cosine-graphs"
 ],
 "lesson": [
  {
   "id": "app-b01",
   "type": "text",
   "md": "# Amplitude, period and phase shift\n\nEvery sinusoid $y=A\\sin(B(x-C))+D$ is the basic sine wave stretched and slid around. Each letter does one job, and reading them off correctly is most of the work on the exam."
  },
  {
   "id": "app-b02",
   "type": "explore",
   "title": "Play with $a$, $b$, $c$ and $d$",
   "plot": {
    "xMin": -3.1416,
    "xMax": 6.2832,
    "yMin": -4,
    "yMax": 4,
    "xPi": true,
    "curves": [
     {
      "expr": "a*sin(b*(x-c))+d",
      "label": "y = a sin(b(x − c)) + d",
      "color": "accent"
     },
     {
      "expr": "sin(x)",
      "label": "y = sin x",
      "color": "gray",
      "dashed": true
     }
    ]
   },
   "params": [
    {
     "name": "a",
     "label": "Amplitude a",
     "min": -3,
     "max": 3,
     "step": 0.5,
     "value": 2
    },
    {
     "name": "b",
     "label": "b (period 2π/b)",
     "min": 0.5,
     "max": 4,
     "step": 0.5,
     "value": 2
    },
    {
     "name": "c",
     "label": "Phase shift c",
     "min": -3.1416,
     "max": 3.1416,
     "step": 0.2618,
     "value": 0.7854
    },
    {
     "name": "d",
     "label": "Vertical shift d",
     "min": -2,
     "max": 2,
     "step": 0.5,
     "value": 0
    }
   ],
   "prompts": [
    "What happens when $a$ becomes negative?",
    "Double $b$: what happens to the period?",
    "Which way does the wave move when $c$ grows?"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "app-b03",
   "type": "table",
   "headers": [
    "Parameter",
    "What it changes",
    "How to read it"
   ],
   "rows": [
    [
     "$A$",
     "Amplitude: the height above the midline",
     "$|A|$"
    ],
    [
     "$B$",
     "Period: the length of one cycle",
     "$\\dfrac{2\\pi}{B}$"
    ],
    [
     "$C$",
     "Phase shift: horizontal slide",
     "right if $C>0$"
    ],
    [
     "$D$",
     "Vertical shift: the midline",
     "$y=D$"
    ]
   ],
   "caption": "$y=A\\sin(B(x-C))+D$"
  },
  {
   "id": "app-b04",
   "type": "predict",
   "question": "What is the period of $y=3\\sin(4x)$?",
   "options": [
    {
     "md": "$\\dfrac{\\pi}{2}$",
     "correct": true,
     "why": "$\\frac{2\\pi}{4}=\\frac{\\pi}{2}$: the wave repeats four times as often."
    },
    {
     "md": "$3$",
     "correct": false,
     "why": "$3$ is the amplitude."
    },
    {
     "md": "$8\\pi$",
     "correct": false,
     "why": "Divide $2\\pi$ by $B$; don't multiply."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "app-b05",
   "type": "example",
   "title": "Reading $y=2\\sin(2x-\\frac{\\pi}{2})+1$",
   "problem": "Find the amplitude, period, phase shift and midline.",
   "steps": [
    {
     "md": "Factor $B$ out: $2x-\\frac{\\pi}{2}=2(x-\\frac{\\pi}{4})$, so $B=2$ and $C=\\frac{\\pi}{4}$.",
     "note": "Without factoring you would read a shift of $\\frac{\\pi}{2}$, the most common mistake here."
    },
    {
     "md": "Amplitude $|A|=2$; period $\\frac{2\\pi}{2}=\\pi$."
    },
    {
     "md": "Phase shift $\\frac{\\pi}{4}$ to the right; midline $y=1$."
    },
    {
     "md": "One cycle runs from $x=\\frac{\\pi}{4}$ to $x=\\frac{5\\pi}{4}$, and the range is $[-1,3]$."
    }
   ],
   "answer": "Amplitude $2$, period $\\pi$, shift $\\frac{\\pi}{4}$ right, midline $y=1$"
  },
  {
   "id": "app-b06",
   "type": "plot",
   "title": "$y=2\\sin(2x-\\frac{\\pi}{2})+1$",
   "xMin": 0,
   "xMax": 6.2832,
   "yMin": -1.6,
   "yMax": 3.6,
   "xPi": true,
   "curves": [
    {
     "expr": "2*sin(2*x-pi/2)+1",
     "label": "y",
     "color": "accent"
    }
   ],
   "lines": [
    {
     "kind": "horizontal",
     "y": "1",
     "color": "gray",
     "label": "midline y = 1"
    }
   ],
   "points": [
    {
     "x": "pi/4",
     "y": "1",
     "label": "start",
     "color": "orange"
    },
    {
     "x": "5*pi/4",
     "y": "1",
     "label": "end",
     "color": "orange"
    },
    {
     "x": "pi/2",
     "y": "3",
     "label": "max",
     "color": "accent"
    }
   ],
   "caption": "One cycle starts at $x=\\frac{\\pi}{4}$, on the midline, going up."
  },
  {
   "id": "app-b07",
   "type": "callout",
   "kind": "mistake",
   "md": "Reading the phase shift before factoring. In $\\sin(2x-\\pi)$ the shift is $\\frac{\\pi}{2}$, not $\\pi$: write it as $\\sin(2(x-\\frac{\\pi}{2}))$ first."
  },
  {
   "id": "app-b08",
   "type": "spot",
   "intro": "Find the phase shift of $y=\\cos(3x+\\pi)$.",
   "lines": [
    "$3x+\\pi=3(x+\\frac{\\pi}{3})$",
    "So $C=-\\frac{\\pi}{3}$.",
    "The graph moves $\\frac{\\pi}{3}$ to the right."
   ],
   "wrongIndex": 2,
   "explanation": "$C<0$ means a shift to the **left**: $\\frac{\\pi}{3}$ units left."
  },
  {
   "id": "app-b09",
   "type": "tryit",
   "title": "Try it",
   "exerciseIDs": [
